{"uid":"ff3184cd9bff21ac","name":"test_steering_during_review_iteration_never_silently_dropped","fullName":"tests.test_e2e#test_steering_during_review_iteration_never_silently_dropped","historyId":"35e25627944161c10a06214e88499a9d","time":{"start":1792071993633,"stop":1792071995812,"duration":2179},"description":"Task 007: steering that lands WHILE a review iteration that would\n    otherwise verify the run is still in flight (i.e. before its\n    ``saw_verified``/pending-steering check even runs, per task 005) must\n    never be silently dropped. The only two acceptable outcomes are: (a) a\n    subsequent worker iteration consumes it before the run goes terminal, or\n    (b) it is loudly reported via the terminal status.json\n    ``unconsumedSteering`` field (task 006). What must NEVER happen is the\n    run going terminal ``succeeded``/``verified`` with the steering file\n    present on disk but absent from BOTH the consumed-steering record AND\n    the terminal status's ``unconsumedSteering`` list -- that would be a\n    silent drop.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 007: steering that lands WHILE a review iteration that would<br />\notherwise verify the run is still in flight (i.e. before its<br />\n<code>saw_verified</code>/pending-steering check even runs, per task 005) must<br />\nnever be silently dropped. The only two acceptable outcomes are: (a) a<br />\nsubsequent worker iteration consumes it before the run goes terminal, or<br />\n(b) it is loudly reported via the terminal status.json<br />\n<code>unconsumedSteering</code> field (task 006). What must NEVER happen is the<br />\nrun going terminal <code>succeeded</code>/<code>verified</code> with the steering file<br />\npresent on disk but absent from BOTH the consumed-steering record AND<br />\nthe terminal status's <code>unconsumedSteering</code> list -- that would be a<br />\nsilent drop.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesSta